 parms←ApplyDefaults parms;defaults;names;missing;name
⍝ Adds to the parameter space `parms` every parameter it lacks, with its default from `CreateParms`.
⍝ A parameter space created by an earlier version lacks the parameters introduced since.\\
⍝ Returns `parms`.
 defaults←CreateParms
 names←' '~¨⍨↓defaults.⎕NL 2
 missing←(0=parms.⎕NC↑names)/names
 :For name :In missing
     ⍎'parms.',name,'←defaults.',name
 :EndFor
